--- ocompiler-2.orig/localtest
+++ ocompiler-2/localtest
@@ -1 +1 @@
-2-5+238
+2-5+239
--- ocompiler-2.orig/o.html
+++ ocompiler-2/o.html
@@ -382,6 +382,8 @@
 	<br>
 	The ":" character represents the size of a long and can be used in the place of a number. Returns 4B on 32-bits, 8B on 64-bits.
 	<br>
+	"?" and a string is the value of the preference (example: ?x_file is x_file preference value).
+	<br>
 	The <b>AfterCall</b> set a value to be tested with zero at the every call and to return if it is not zero.
 	<br>
 	<b>AfterCallImport</b> is used in objects to import an extern defined AfterCall.
@@ -978,7 +980,7 @@ format elfobj64<br>
 <p>Black = 1 byte. <span class="blue">Blue = 4 bytes = data.</span> <span class="red">Red = string = data[+byte(s)].</span> <span class="green">Green = replacement.</span></p>
 <p>There are at least two options at the '*' wildcard from there. '{}' is an enumeration.</p>
 <p>First long(4 bytes) is null or offset of entry which will be at the end.</p>
-<p>Xfile_noignore at ocompiler is ^ sign before the command, and at otoc will noignore a tagIgnore argument.</p>
+<p>Xfile_noignore at ocompiler is '^' sign before the command, and at otoc will noignore a tagIgnore argument. Xfile_yesignore at compiler is '!' sign before the command and at otoc will ignore the command.</p>
